Question 14You are designing test cases based on the following decision table:
So far you have designed the following test cases:
1. TC1: 19-year-old, unregistered man with no experience;
2. TC2: 65-year-old, unregistered woman with 4 years of experience;
3. TC3: 30-year-old, registered man with no experience;
4. TC4: 65-year-old, registered woman with 4 years of experience;
What is the decision table coverage achieved by these test cases?

Your team uses planning poker to estimate the test effort for a newly required feature.
Given the following user story: “As a user, I want to be able to send and receive messages easily on the platform to communicate with other users in a convenient and efficient manner”
• Each estimator has a deck of cards with values similar to the Fibonacci sequence (1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21)
• If someone that a user story is big, they assign an estimate of 100;
Two iterations of the planning poker sessions have occurred:
During the first iteration of the planning poker session, the following story points were given:
• Scrum master: 13;
• Developer: 21;
• Tester: 100
During the second iteration of the planning poker session, the following story points were given:
• Scrum master: 21;
• Developer: 100;
• Tester: 100
What is the best outcome for this planning poker session, assuming the time limit of the planning poker sessions for estimating this story has been reached?
